//? Title: ECG and smartwatch CNNs:original channels and visible tensor fits
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Complete strided residual CNNs learn from genuine ECG200 and six-channel BasicMotions records. Explicit fitting-only normalization,class-weighted CE,SGD references,all42 Adam updates and every held-out source-class diagnostic reveal both behavior and failures.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.9_1d_convolutions/ecg_sensor_cnn.cpp`.

> The method

Preserve original source records,channels and class order. Compute normalization and class weights only on fitting tensors,then train three strided residual stages with an explicit weighted objective. Restore paired learned/channel state for raw-signal-only prediction,and compare fixed SGD references with full confusion,balanced recall,macroF1 and tie-aware binary AUROC.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.tikz > build/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.svg build/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.dvi > build/ecg_sensor_cnn_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
