> Original ECG and six-channel smartwatch observations

Retain the complete official100-record ECG200 and40-record BasicMotions test
sets. Seed407 shuffles each official training class and holds rounded20% for
validation:ECG80fit/20val and BasicMotions32fit/8val. Original source-record IDs
remain disjoint,but there are no verified patient/participant holdouts.
ECG has96 samples and one channel;the original -1/+1 class codes become0/1.
Do not guess a clinical meaning for either code. These are released source
values,not a claim of unprocessed millivolt sensor acquisition.

BasicMotions has100 samples,six channels:accelerometer x/y/z then gyroscope
x/y/z. Original TS class inventory order is Standing,Running,Walking,Badminton,
which becomes0/1/2/3. Preserve this order in every metric and confusion plot.
Fitting-only channel population mean/std and class weights N/(K*count) are
tensor reductions,rounded once to Float32. Test values never estimate them.

Pinned official archives and exact original values/IDs are retained in the
source manifests. An independent NumPy validation reads **different original
archive formats**—TXT for ECG/GunPoint and six separate ARFF channels for
BasicMotions—and verifies every value,label and ID against prepared TS ingress.
This separate source oracle is never used for report fitting or preprocessing.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("signals", cache);
}
```
