> Three strided residual stages preserve every channel

Detach saved per-channel mean/std,then apply three stages. Each stage uses
5x1 stride2/ReLU followed by3x1 stride1,plus a learned1x1 stride2 skip and
ReLU after addition. TensorFlow SAME determines the even/odd stride phase.
Widths are base/2base/4base;global time mean feeds a linear class head.
Full base64 and compact8 both retain20 learned leaves and two per-channel
normalization arrays. No BN,dropout or hidden optimizer is present.
Native checks execute both full graphs and every learned derivative,plus
independent finite differences for all171 tiny strided multichannel coordinates.
```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  std::print("| source | base | learned values | leaves | state arrays | stage1 | stage2 | "
             "stage3 | head |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|---|---|---|\n");
  for (bool motion : {false, true})
    for (int base : {64, 8}) {
      n::ParameterStore p(613), state(617);
      m::SensorConfig c{motion ? 6 : 1, motion ? 4 : 2, base};
      const auto out = m::SensorCnn(p, state, n::ones({2, motion ? 100 : 96, c.channels}), c);
      std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
                 motion ? "BasicMotions" : "ECG200", base, p.count(), p.size(), state.size(),
                 out.stages[0].shape(), out.stages[1].shape(), out.stages[2].shape(),
                 out.logits.shape());
    }
}
