The selected ECG model reaches accuracy.410000,balanced recall.539062 and
macroF1.347273. It gets all36 source-class0 records but only5/64class1
records correct. Its ranking AUROC.784288 does not rescue poor argmax
classification. Standardized1NN reaches.900000 accuracy and SGD centroid
.750000;the untrained/count prior reaches.640000.

BasicMotions accuracy/balanced recall is.275000,below1NN.500000 and
SGD centroid.425000. Learned recalls are0/.3/0/.8:Standing and Walking
both fail entirely. The report therefore claims no useful learned-model
advantage despite improved fitting losses and nonzero channel sensitivity.

> Independent validation and limits

Eight native tests verify all171tiny strided residual parameter coordinates
against independent host finite differences,full graphs/every learned gradient
for both sources,extreme weighted CE and every logit derivative,known imbalance/
confusion/F1/recall/AUROC ties,every original sample/ID/label/fitting statistic,
every reference/metric value,explicit SGD centroid parity,input gradients and
all channel interventions. Invalid std,missing class and undefined AUROC reject.
Every public Doxygen example compiles/runs and the original two-dataset
three-epoch workflow executes. Standalone headers and source oracles pass.

This is a small source-record-held-out teaching fit,not verified patient or
participant separation. Original acquisition dependencies remain. Numerical
sensitivity,source imbalance compensation and lower fitting loss do not
establish useful held-out classification;all class outcomes remain visible.

> Annotated confusion counts

The following program replots the complete frozen evaluation counts printed in the
predictor tables above. It reproduces those recorded measurements without refitting
or re-evaluating the model. `ConfusionMatrix::from_counts` owns the integer tensor
counts and `save_svg` labels every cell. True class zero is the **top** row and
predicted class zero the left column. Counts are exact; colors use the observed
count range. Source class meanings remain those declared for the dataset above.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/ecg_sensor_cnn_confusion_api_0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  {
    const auto counts = n::from_vector(
        std::vector<std::int64_t>{0, 9, 0, 1, 0, 3, 0, 7, 0, 1, 0, 9, 0, 2, 0, 8}, {4, 4});
    const auto matrix = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(counts);
    if (std::abs(matrix.accuracy() - 0.275) > 1e-5)
      return 1;
    matrix.save_svg(
        "build/ecg_sensor_cnn_confusion_api_1.svg",
        {.title = "ecg sensor cnn / learned / 2", .cell_size = 52, .font_size = 13});
    std::print("Recorded evaluation 2: 40 observations; accuracy {:.6f}.\n", matrix.accuracy());
  }
  {
    const auto counts = n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{36, 0, 59, 5}, {2, 2});
    const auto matrix = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(counts);
    if (std::abs(matrix.accuracy() - 0.41) > 1e-5)
      return 1;
    matrix.save_svg(
        "build/ecg_sensor_cnn_confusion_api_0.svg",
        {.title = "ecg sensor cnn / learned / 1", .cell_size = 52, .font_size = 13});
    std::print("Recorded evaluation 1: 100 observations; accuracy {:.6f}.\n", matrix.accuracy());
  }
}
